# Env files, without exception. `.env.docker` was the one missing from this list,
# and because settings.py loads it whenever it exists, its presence decided two
# things on a machine that had an untracked copy (the Mac) and not on one that
# did not (dell): the image layer carried a real SECRET_KEY and POSTGRES_PASSWORD
# at /app/.env.docker, and the collectstatic in the Dockerfile succeeded there
# while `ImproperlyConfigured: SECRET_KEY must be set in production` killed it on
# the server. The exception was invisible because that RUN ended in `|| true`.
# An image must carry no secret, and the same commit must build the same image
# wherever it is built.
.env
.env.*
*.sqlite3
db.sqlite3
*.log
.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea
